    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Ok, thanks. I'm curious about your reasoning on Post 3 though. You said it passes because it doesn't target protected characteristics, but isn't the language \"actn like a clown\" and \"trippin\" often used in a way that can be seen as aggressive or hostile? Some of our testers flagged that type of vernacular as inherently higher risk for escalation. Why do you think it's safe compared to more standard English insults?",
