      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should be very careful about policing dialect, as that is often a proxy for race and culture. Over-moderating slang to achieve a \"cleaner\" feel is usually a way to enforce a specific, often white, standard of acceptable speech. If you start flagging based on dialect alone, you risk silencing legitimate voices and creating an exclusionary platform.",
